(Chapter 3: Photosynthesis) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light) Tj
T* (energy into chemical energy stored in glucose. It takes place in the) Tj
T* (chloroplast, an organelle that contains the green pigment chlorophyll.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Photosynthesis occurs in two stages. The first stage is the) Tj
T* (light-dependent reactions, which take place in the thylakoid membrane.) Tj
T* (Here, chlorophyll absorbs light and water is split in a step called) Tj
T* (photolysis, releasing oxygen as a by-product and producing ATP and) Tj
T* (NADPH.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The second stage is the Calvin cycle, also called the light-independent) Tj
T* (reactions, which takes place in the stroma. The Calvin cycle uses the) Tj
T* (ATP and NADPH from the first stage to fix carbon dioxide into glucose.) Tj
